Today's earnings data from National Bank shows 26% EPS growth alongside two dividend

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:56.880
increases in the past year, creating a setup where the payout ratio remains below 40%.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.640
Investors can apply this by pulling the latest quarterly results into a simple spreadsheet,

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.320
calculating the forward PE and comparing it against the five-year average for the same name.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.960
The approach works best when sector rotation is not already pressuring the group, which

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.280
